---
// The site's icon set, drawn once per page and used through <Icon>.
// Drawn to the XP Visual Guidelines (icons.htm):
//   - one 48x48 drawing that also reads at 32 and 16;
//   - light from the upper left, soft rounded edges, a darker outline
//     so each icon holds up on white, blue and the desktop alike;
//   - colours from the guide's icon palette;
//   - full icons carry the guide's drop shadow (angle 135, distance 2,
//     size 2, black), toolbar and navigation glyphs do not;
//   - navigation buttons are round-cornered badges with white signs:
//     green to go, yellow for the gentler "high impact" action;
//   - no letters, words, hands, faces or Windows flags.
// The sprite must stay rendered (not display: none) or the gradients
// inside it stop painting in Firefox and Chromium.
---

<svg class="icon-sprite" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
	<defs>
		<filter id="xp-ds" x="-20%" y="-20%" width="150%" height="150%" color-interpolation-filters="sRGB">
			<feDropShadow dx="1.41" dy="1.41" stdDeviation="1" flood-color="#000" flood-opacity="0.45" />
		</filter>

		<linearGradient id="g-paper" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
